{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Braking Engine.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Braking Engine.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"braking engine braking engine","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Braking Engine.md","fileName":"Braking Engine.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Braking Engine","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Systems]] [[Game Economies]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Systems","Game Economies","Balancing Loop","Boosting Engine","advancedgamedesign.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Braking Engine.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Braking Engine.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"braking engine braking engine","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Braking Engine.md","fileName":"Braking Engine.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Braking Engine","heading":"Braking Engine","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A braking engine is a predominantly [[Balancing Loop|balancing]] structure that drains a resource or reduces its future rate of gain. It creates friction that regulates progress and counteracts a reinforcing engine.\n\nBrakes can preserve competition and pacing, but excessive friction leaves the player unable to act and can stop the game. They are therefore usually subsidiary loops within a [[Boosting Engine]], economy, or progression system.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Systems","Game Economies","Balancing Loop","Boosting Engine","advancedgamedesign.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Braking Engine.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Braking Engine.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"braking engine braking engine","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Braking Engine.md","fileName":"Braking Engine.md"